================================================================================
TESTING FOCAL TVERSKY LOSS
================================================================================

Why focal_tversky for this dataset:
  1. Severe class imbalance: 92% background, 8% foreground
  2. Small objects: Microbeads are tiny relative to image size
  3. Hard examples: Overlapping beads, varied illumination

Focal Tversky parameters:
  α=0.7: Penalize false negatives 2.3× more than false positives
  β=0.3: Tolerate some over-segmentation to catch all beads
  γ=1.33: Focus on hard examples (paper-recommended value)
================================================================================

Model: UNet
Parameters: 31,401,345

Starting training with focal_tversky loss...
Watch for: Validation Jaccard should stay > 10% (vs 3% with combined loss)

